  - NRVS
  - pDOS
abstract: >-
  PeakCheck determines peaks in a reference x/y data set (e.g. a summed
  spectrum) and checks whether those peaks are present in one or more component
  data sets (e.g. sub-spectra). It uses area-normalised Voigt/Gaussian/Lorentzian
  profiles (true Voigt via the Faddeeva function), rolling-minimum background
  subtraction and a weighted non-negative least-squares amplitude fit, and ships
  with a Tkinter GUI and a TOML-driven headless mode.
